<title>BELGIUM: Santer reiterates call for TENs approval.</title>
<headline>Santer reiterates call for TENs approval.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Commission President Jacques Santer on Wednesday called for EU finance ministers to approve a plan to boost spending on trans-European road and rail links (TENs), a key element in his bid to create more jobs.</p>
<p>&quot;TENs should not be seen as just part of an employment plan,&quot; he told a news conference.</p>
<p>&quot;They are an investment for the future which will help us operate as a proper, common, integrated market,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>An informal meeting of EU finance ministers in Dublin last weekend showed scant enthusiasm for the projects, which would require them to put aside a billion Ecus ($1.26 billion).</p>
<p>The projects include high-speed trains between Paris and Cologne and between Frankfurt and London, plus motorways in Greece, Spain and Portugal.</p>
<p>Santer said he was convinced that the European Council in Dublin in December would resolve the matter.</p>
<p>The ECOFIN Council will take up Santer's plan on October 14.</p>
</text>
